1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,200
If you've started Wegovy, Zepbound, or Mounjaro and suddenly feel dizzy or lightheaded, it's not just the weight loss talking.

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:09,280
Three real changes are behind it.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:15,200
Dizziness shows up in up to one in ten people on these medications, most often in the first few weeks.

4
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:21,600
Appetite suppression, fluid loss from nausea and diarrhea, and a sudden drop in blood pressure are usually why.

5
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:27,360
First, these drugs suppress appetite so strongly that daily food intake drops sharply.

6
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:34,160
Less fuel means your blood sugar runs low, especially if you're also taking insulin or other diabetes medication.

7
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:38,560
Eat small, protein-rich meals every few hours instead of skipping meals.

8
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:43,920
Second, nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea pull fluid and sodium out of your body fast.

9
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:45,680
Don't just sip plain water.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,520
Add an electrolyte drink or salty broth to replace what you're losing.

11
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:53,440
Finally, rapid weight loss lowers blood pressure on its own.

12
00:00:53,760 --> 00:01:01,120
If you're already on blood pressure medication, your old dose may now be too strong, and standing up too fast can trigger a sudden head rush.

13
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:05,840
Check your blood pressure regularly and ask your doctor whether your dosage still fits.

14
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:11,680
Track these three causes, and dizziness from your weight loss injection becomes something you can manage with confidence.
